diff --git a/CHANGELOG.rst b/CHANGELOG.rst
index a5d78ef..7879359 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.rst
+++ b/CHANGELOG.rst
@@ -10,6 +10,25 @@ The third digit is only for regressions.
 Backward-incompatible changes:
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 
+- Replace the CFFI implementation with typed Rust ownership. Context trust-store
+  proxies reject mutation after the first Connection, including proxies retained
+  before that Connection was created. Concurrent or reentrant native operations
+  on one Connection raise RuntimeError.
+- Pending writes require identical bytes on retry, including when native moving
+  buffer mode is enabled. ``sendall`` retains its progress across retry errors.
+  Fatal TLS failures prevent further native I/O on that Connection.
+- SNI, information and key-log callback exceptions propagate to the initiating
+  operation instead of using a process-global exception hook. Callback metadata
+  is a snapshot; SNI context selection is applied after the callback returns.
+- ``set_tmp_ecdh`` configures actual TLS groups and rejects curves unavailable to
+  TLS. Cryptographic curve support alone no longer implies TLS group support.
+- Deprecated ``OpenSSL.rand.add`` mixes additional input without crediting the
+  caller's entropy estimate. The native backend obtains entropy from the OS.
+- LibreSSL does not implement TLS 1.3 CA-name hints. Configuring a nonempty
+  client CA list requires explicitly limiting the Context to TLS 1.2 first;
+  subsequently raising the maximum version is rejected. Key-log configuration
+  also reports LibreSSL's unimplemented native callback instead of accepting it.
+
 - ``OpenSSL.crypto.X509.set_serial_number()`` now raises ``ValueError`` for a negative serial number, which
   `RFC 5280 section 4.1.2.2 <https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5280#section-4.1.2.2>`_ does not permit.
   Passing one previously crashed the interpreter.
